==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|rakia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|sh|rakija}}/{{m|sh|sc=Cyrl|ракија}}, from {{der|en|ota|راقی|tr=rakı}}, assumed from {{der|en|ar|عَرَق|t=[[sweat]]; [[wine]]}} (as rakija or wine vapor drops are similar to drops of sweat). {{doublet|en|raki}}.
{{root|en|ar|ع ر ق‎}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɑːkɪə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A strong [[distilled]] [[alcohol|alcoholic]] [[beverage]] made from various fruits, varieties of which (such as [[slivovitz]]) are found across the Balkans and the Mediterranean. {{qualifier|Compare ''[[brandy]]''.}}

